                    <div><h1 property="headline" class="uk-margin-remove-bottom uk-article-title">Westchester County Board of Elections</h1></div><div class="uk-panel uk-margin"><div style="background-color: rgba(212, 211, 214, .25); width: 100%; float: left; clear: both; padding: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
<p>The <strong>Westchester County Board of Elections</strong> has relocated to:<br /><strong>445 Hamilton Avenue, 8th Floor, White Plains, NY 10601</strong></p>
<p><strong>All phone numbers and email addresses will remain the same. We look forward to continuing to serve the public at our new location.</strong></p>
<p><strong>2026 Elections</strong></p>
<p>General Election – Tuesday, November 3, 2026<br />Polls open 6:00 a.m. – 9:00 p.m.<br />Early Voting: Saturday, October 24th – Sunday, November 1st</p>
<p><strong>Our office will be open for Vote By Mail Department Extended Hours</strong><br />Tuesday, October 20, 2026 until 8:00 PM <br />Thursday, October 22, 2026 until 8:00 PM <br />Saturday, October 24, 2026 from 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM <br />Tuesday, October 27, 2026 until 8:00 PM <br />Thursday, October 29, 2026 until 8:00 PM<br />Saturday, October 31, 2026 from 9:00 AM until 6:00 PM</p>
<p>This is for the purpose of obtaining an absentee/early vote by mail ballot/application and dropping off completed absentee/early vote by mail ballots.
</p>
<p>Last Day to Register to Vote for General Election is <strong>Saturday, October 24, 2026</strong>.<br /><strong>Mail Registration:</strong> Applications must be received by the Westchester County Board of Elections no later than <strong>October 24, 2026</strong> to be eligible to vote in the General Election.<br /><strong>In Person Registration:</strong> You may register at the Westchester County Board of Elections, any Early Voting sites by completing an Affidavit Ballot form, and any state agency participating in the National Voter Registration Act, but, to be eligible to vote in the General Election, your application must be received no later than <strong>October 24, 2026</strong>.</p>
<p><a href="/images/stories/pdfs/2026/2026-candidate-list-no-address.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2026 Unofficial General Election Candidate List</a></p>
</div>
<p>We are committed to keeping you aware of changes to the election law and how those changes affect voting in Westchester. Our office is here to assist you in any way we can.</p>
<p>Westchester County works hard to encourage and protect your right to vote as a United States citizen. From the county’s Board of Elections, you can <a href="/find-polling-place" target="_self">find your ballot and polling place</a>, <a href="/voting/register-to-vote">register to vote</a> and learn about <a href="/voting/request-an-election-ballot" target="_self">how to request an election ballot</a>.</p>
<p>You can learn how to <a href="/run-for-office/overview" target="_self">run for office</a> or obtain county, state and federal <a href="/run-for-office/campaign-finance-forms">financial disclosure statements</a>.</p>
<p>For additional voting information, visit <a href="http://www.vote411.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Link opens Vote411 Web site in a new window">Vote411</a>, an interactive Web site created and maintained by the League of Women Voters. The site supplies personalized ballots and polling locations simply by entering your home address.</p>
<p><a href="mailto:tmc1@westchestergov.com; wgm1@westchestercountyny.gov?subject=Comments to the Board of Elections" target="_self">Send your comments</a> to the Board of Elections.</p></div>
                
            
        
    
</div>
<div class="uk-width-1-5@m uk-flex-first@m">
    
        
            
            
            
                
